  "paper_id": "eurosys-2023-diagnosing-kernel-concurrency-failures-with-aitia-d543c992",
  "title": "Diagnosing Kernel Concurrency Failures with AITIA",
  "abstract": "Kernel concurrency failures are notoriously difficult to identify and diagnose their fundamental reason, the root cause. Kernel concurrency bugs frequently involve challenging patterns such as multi-variable races, data races with asynchronous kernel threads, and pervasive benign races. We perform an in-depth study of real-world kernel concurrency bugs and elicit three requirements: comprehensiveness, pattern-agnostic, and conciseness.",
